{#-
  Changelog template rendered by commitizen (`cz bump --changelog` and
  `cz changelog`; selected by `template` in .cz.toml).

  `tree` holds the releases newest first, each with `version`, `date`, and
  `changes` grouped by type; `repo_url` comes from `extras` in .cz.toml.
  A release without a date is the not-yet-tagged block, so it gets no
  release link.

  The release workflow reads the newest version from this file, so the
  version header line is the only place a version string may appear twice
  (link text + URL) -- keep other links off that line.
-#}
{% for entry in tree %}

## {% if entry.date %}[{{ entry.version }}]({{ repo_url }}/releases/tag/{{ entry.version }}) ({{ entry.date }}){% else %}{{ entry.version }}{% endif %}

{% for change_key, changes in entry.changes.items() %}

{% if change_key %}
### {{ change_key }}
{% endif %}

{% for change in changes %}
- {% if change.breaking %}**BREAKING**: {% endif %}{% if change.scope %}**{{ change.scope }}**: {% endif %}{{ change.message }} ([`{{ change.sha1[:7] }}`]({{ repo_url }}/commit/{{ change.sha1 }}))
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}
